    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286">

                <pb facs="0287" n="171" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg171"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/1146.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-06T16:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 6, 1912—4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>With reference to your telegram of March 4, 1 p.m. After consulting colleagues I
                    have telegraphed for the additional troops.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Calhoun.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Note.</hi>—The disturbances having subsided, no
                        further correspondence appears on this subject.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
